%% title: Running Tests from Slack — Overview
%% description: The short version — three pieces, and who talks to whom when someone types the command

flowchart TD
    classDef person fill:#0F766E,stroke:#5EEAD4,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff;
    classDef slack fill:#4A154B,stroke:#fff,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff;
    classDef edge fill:#1E293B,stroke:#F59E0B,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff;
    classDef runner fill:#0F172A,stroke:#38BDF8,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff;
    classDef note fill:#111827,stroke:#64748B,stroke-width:1px,color:#CBD5E1;

    P["🧑 <b>Anyone on the team</b><br/>No GitHub account, no VPN,<br/>no need to know pytest"]:::person

    S["💬 <b>Slack</b><br/><code>/testauto runtests checkout staging</code><br/><i>which suite · which server</i>"]:::slack

    E["🌐 <b>Edge server</b><br/>The only public piece.<br/>Checks the request is genuine<br/>and allowed, then parks it on<br/>a list of work to do.<br/><i>Runs no tests itself.</i>"]:::edge

    T["🖥️ <b>Test server</b><br/>Lives inside our network.<br/>Asks for work, runs the suite,<br/>and reports what happened."]:::runner

    OUT["📢 <b>#testing in Slack</b><br/>started · finished ·<br/><i>42 passed, 1 failed, 3m 12s</i>"]:::slack

    WHY["🔒 <b>Why the arrows point that way</b><br/>The test server always calls <b>out</b>.<br/>Nothing outside ever calls in, so<br/>there is no door to knock on."]:::note

    P -->|"types the command"| S
    S -->|"1 · sends it on"| E
    E -.->|"2 · replies in under 3 seconds: <i>queued</i>"| S
    T -->|"3 · anything for me?"| E
    E -->|"4 · here is the job"| T
    T -->|"5 · runs the suite,<br/>then says how it went"| OUT
    OUT -->|"everyone can read it"| P

    WHY -.- T
